  "source": "NEET 2020",
  "question": "A short electric dipole has a dipole moment of $16 \\times 10^{-9}$ C m. The electric potential due to the dipole at a point at a distance of $0.6$ m from the centre of the dipole, situated on a line making an angle of $60°$ with the dipole axis is : $\\left(\\dfrac{1}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0} = 9 \\times 10^9\\ \\text{N m}^2/\\text{C}^2\\right)$",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
