  "answer": "B",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$$V = \\frac{1}{4\\pi\\epsilon_0}\\frac{p\\cos\\theta}{r^2} = \\frac{9 \\times 10^9 \\times 16 \\times 10^{-9} \\times 0.5}{(0.6)^2} = \\frac{72}{0.36} = 200\\ \\text{V}$$",
